-- הסכם קיבוצי (שטר בוררות) מיום 1.2.2007 — שיעור השחיקה ודרך חישובה: the
-- arbitration deed between the employers (the State, the Centre of Local
-- Government for the local authorities, and the three large cities) and
-- both teachers' organisations, הסתדרות המורים and ארגון המורים, jointly. It
-- sends to arbitration their dispute over the erosion of the teachers' pay
-- against the engineers' under the wage agreements of 1993–1995, for
-- 1.1.99–31.12.06 only (§2); names a panel of three and how its head
-- decides between the other two (§3); what the award rests on, its two
-- parts, the 0.5% a year already paid and the deadlines (§4); the head
-- arbitrator's fee and the Arbitration Law (§§5–6); exhaustion of claims
-- (§7) and the 1993–1995 agreements (§8); and the Treasury's summary of the
-- same day on the erosion database, held with it.
--
-- WHAT IT CARRIES OUT: the erosion check of the wage agreement of
-- 11.5.1993 (§8, imported), whose shared database (§8(ב)(5)) is the data
-- the panel decides on (§4.1; finding F-erosion-deed-a on the section the
-- deed names). The agreement of 1994 and the Oz organisation's agreements
-- of 1993–1995 are not encoded here; the deed names them only as the
-- source of the dispute.
--
-- WHAT CAME OF IT: the award for 1999–2001 was given on 22.5.2007, and the
-- second period was settled by agreement instead — ארגון המורים's of
-- 24.1.2008 (l4/agreements/oz-latmura/2008-01-24_oz-latmura_erosion-arbitration-award.l4)
-- and הסתדרות המורים's of 21.2.2008
-- (l4/agreements/teachers-general/2008-02-21_teachers_erosion-arbitration-4pct-2002-2007.l4),
-- each of which stops this arbitration for 2002–2006 save one question.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `1993-05-11_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1993`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי (שטר בוררות) — שיעור השחיקה ודרך חישובה (1.2.2007)`

DECLARE `erosion arbitration deed action` IS ONE OF
    `set out the dissenting view in every decision and in the erosion award`
    `give a reasoned erosion award in two parts`
    `address how the erosion award is applied to the teachers' pay`
    `make efforts for the first erosion award by 15.3.2007`
    `give the second erosion award`
    `pay half the agreed erosion arbitrator's fee`
    `pay half the cost of running the erosion database for 2002–2006`
    `deduct the organisations' half of the erosion database's cost from the sums due them for 2007`
    `send a copy of an erosion database request to the other side`
    `object to an erosion database request that is not about erosion`
    `pass the results of an erosion database request to all three at once`

-- akn:preamble The deed's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The Treasury's incoming-mail stamp of 11.2.2007; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The Haifa municipality's incoming stamp of 14.2.2007, partly illegible; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 A filing mark and barcode; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 Its subtitle, "an arbitration deed"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 The first party, the State, and who represents it (the wages commissioner and the Ministry's Director-General); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The Centre of Local Government, for every local authority save the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 The three large cities and who represents them; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 The second party, הסתדרות המורים, and its secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 The union's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 15.5.2007, number 104/2007; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The third party, ארגון המורים, and its chairman, the line's start illegible; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 The organisation's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 The two organisations' joint short name, "ארגוני המורים"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p21 The Treasury's incoming-mail stamp of 22.2.2007; no rule.

-- ¶6: the day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p6
`the erosion arbitration deed was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2007

-- The recitals: the parties disagree on how the collective agreements of
-- 1993–1995 apply to the check of the teachers' pay erosion against the
-- engineers' for the time from 1.1.99 (¶17); the three months agreed for
-- discussing it brought no agreement (¶18); and they agreed to send the
-- disagreement on the rate of erosion and how it is computed, for
-- 1.1.99–31.12.06 only, to arbitration (¶19) — §2's matter.
@ref akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18 akn:preamble/p19
`months the parties had agreed to discuss the erosion dispute` MEANS 3

§§ `1 המבוא`

@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p1
`the erosion arbitration deed's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 בוררות`

-- §2: the matter sent to arbitration — the rate of erosion of the teaching
-- employees' pay against the engineers' and how it is computed, under the
-- wage agreements of 1993, 1994 and 1995, for 1.1.99–31.12.06 only.
@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a year the erosion arbitration covers` y IF
    y AT LEAST 1999 AND y AT MOST 2006

#ASSERT `a year the erosion arbitration covers` 1999
#ASSERT `a year the erosion arbitration covers` 2006
#ASSERT NOT `a year the erosion arbitration covers` 2007

§§ `3 הבוררים`

-- 3.1–3.3: the panel — שלום גרניט for both organisations jointly, מוטי
-- מרוז for the employers, and פרופ' מוטי מירוני, the third, "the agreed
-- arbitrator".
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-2 akn:art_3__para_3-3
`the erosion arbitrators named in the deed` MEANS
    LIST "שלום גרניט (מטעם ארגוני המורים במשותף)",
         "מוטי מרוז (מטעם המעסיקים)",
         "פרופ' מוטי מירוני (הבורר המוסכם)"

DECLARE `erosion award period` IS ONE OF
    `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001`
    `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006`

-- 3.4 ¶2–¶3: "the decisive gap" — 4% for 1.1.99–31.12.01, 3.5% for
-- 1.1.02–31.12.06.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p4
GIVEN p IS AN `erosion award period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the decisive gap of the erosion arbitration for` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001` THEN 4%
    WHEN `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006` THEN 3.5%

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the gap between the two other arbitrators' rates` a b IS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a MINUS b ELSE b MINUS a

-- 3.4: the agreed arbitrator heads the panel and his view decides between
-- the arbitrators. Where the gap between the other two's rates of erosion
-- for a period does not exceed the decisive gap, he decides that period by
-- the view of one of them; where it exceeds it ("עולה על", above and not
-- at: convention thresholds.above), he may decide otherwise than both.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4
GIVEN p IS AN `erosion award period`, a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreed erosion arbitrator may depart from both views` p a b IF
    `the gap between the two other arbitrators' rates` a b GREATER THAN `the decisive gap of the erosion arbitration for` p

GIVEN p IS AN `erosion award period`, a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, decided IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreed erosion arbitrator's rate is open to him` p a b decided IF
        decided EQUALS a
    OR decided EQUALS b
    OR `the agreed erosion arbitrator may depart from both views` p a b

#ASSERT NOT `the agreed erosion arbitrator's rate is open to him` `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001` (2%) (6%) (4%)
#ASSERT `the agreed erosion arbitrator's rate is open to him` `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006` (2%) (6%) (4%)
#ASSERT `the agreed erosion arbitrator's rate is open to him` `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001` (2%) (6%) (6%)

-- 3.5: an arbitrator whose view the agreed arbitrator did not adopt sets
-- it out in every decision and in the award.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5
`the dissenting erosion arbitrator's view` MEANS
    PARTY `the erosion arbitrators`
    MUST  `set out the dissenting view in every decision and in the erosion award`

§§ `4 פסק הבוררות`

-- 4.1: the panel decides on the pay data in the database set up for the
-- erosion check — the shared database of the agreement of 11.5.1993
-- (`setting up the 1993 erosion database`, imported). The deed says the
-- database is "as said in §5" of that agreement; its §5 is "תוספת 1993",
-- and the database is set up in §8(ב)(5). Finding F-erosion-deed-a; read
-- by the subject (convention reading.cross-reference-subject).
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_4-1
`the database the erosion arbitration decides on` MEANS `setting up the 1993 erosion database`

`the section of 11.5.1993 the deed's §4.1 names` MEANS 5
`the section of 11.5.1993 that pays the 1993 supplement` MEANS 5
`the section of 11.5.1993 that sets up the erosion database` MEANS 8

-- F-erosion-deed-a's evidence: the section the deed names is the one that
-- pays "תוספת 1993", and the database is another section's.
`§4.1 of the erosion arbitration deed names the section of the 1993 supplement, not the database's` MEANS
        `the section of 11.5.1993 the deed's §4.1 names` EQUALS `the section of 11.5.1993 that pays the 1993 supplement`
    AND NOT `the section of 11.5.1993 the deed's §4.1 names` EQUALS `the section of 11.5.1993 that sets up the erosion database`
#ASSERT `§4.1 of the erosion arbitration deed names the section of the 1993 supplement, not the database's`

-- 4.2: the panel decides the rate only once, in the agreed arbitrator's
-- view, it holds a full analysis and full results of the database's data.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2
GIVEN `the agreed arbitrator holds a full analysis of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the erosion panel may decide the rate` `the agreed arbitrator holds a full analysis of the data` IF
    `the agreed arbitrator holds a full analysis of the data`

-- 4.3: a reasoned award in two parts only — (1) 1.1.99–31.12.01, (2)
-- 1.1.02–31.12.06.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2
`the parts of the erosion award` MEANS
    LIST `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001`, `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006`

`the erosion award in parts` MEANS
    PARTY `the erosion arbitrators`
    MUST  `give a reasoned erosion award in two parts`

-- 4.4: each part treats each year of its period on its own.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4
GIVEN p IS AN `erosion award period`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the years an erosion award treats one by one` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the first erosion period, 1999 to 2001` THEN LIST 1999, 2000, 2001
    WHEN `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006` THEN LIST 2002, 2003, 2004, 2005, 2006

#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD `a year the erosion arbitration covers` y)
            (`the years an erosion award treats one by one` `the second erosion period, 2002 to 2006`)

-- 4.5: the payment for erosion already paid for 1999–2005, 0.5% a year, is
-- taken off the rate of erosion set for each of those years. The deed puts
-- no floor under the result, and §8(ב)(1) of 11.5.1993 itself speaks of an
-- erosion supplement "paid or set off", so it is computed as printed.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-5
`the erosion already paid each year, 1999 to 2005` MEANS 0.5%

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, `the rate the award sets for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the erosion rate the award leaves for a year` y `the rate the award sets for the year` IS
    IF y AT LEAST 1999 AND y AT MOST 2005
    THEN `the rate the award sets for the year` MINUS `the erosion already paid each year, 1999 to 2005`
    ELSE `the rate the award sets for the year`

#ASSERT `the erosion rate the award leaves for a year` 2003 (2%) EQUALS (1.5%)
#ASSERT `the erosion rate the award leaves for a year` 2006 (2%) EQUALS (2%)

-- 4.6: the awards say how they are applied to the teachers' pay.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6
`the erosion award's application` MEANS
    PARTY `the erosion arbitrators`
    MUST  `address how the erosion award is applied to the teachers' pay`

-- 4.7: the parties and the panel make efforts for the award for 1999–2001
-- to be given by 15.3.07 — an effort, not a deadline.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-7
`the target day for the first erosion award` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2007

`efforts for the first erosion award` MEANS
    PARTY `the erosion arbitrators`
    MUST  `make efforts for the first erosion award by 15.3.2007`

-- 4.8: the award for 1.1.02–31.12.06 is due by 31.12.07; the panel may ask
-- the parties for half a year more, to 30.6.08; if it is not given by
-- 30.6.08, each party may demand that the arbitration for that period be
-- cancelled. The deadline the panel works to is 31.12.07 unless the
-- extension is had; the right to cancel runs from 30.6.08 either way.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-8
GIVEN `the panel had the half-year extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for the second erosion award` `the panel had the half-year extension` IS
    IF `the panel had the half-year extension` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2008 ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2007

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the second award was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party may demand the second erosion period's arbitration be cancelled` d `the second award was given` IF
        NOT `the second award was given`
    AND NOT d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2008)

#ASSERT `a party may demand the second erosion period's arbitration be cancelled` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2008) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a party may demand the second erosion period's arbitration be cancelled` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2008) FALSE

§§ `5 שכר הבוררים`

-- 5.1: the agreed arbitrator's fee is paid by the parties, half by the
-- employers' side and half by the organisations'. Of the other two
-- arbitrators' fees the deed says nothing.
@ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5__para_5-1
`each side's share of the agreed erosion arbitrator's fee` MEANS 50%

`the agreed erosion arbitrator's fee` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay half the agreed erosion arbitrator's fee`

-- 5.2: the Arbitration Law does not apply to the arbitrators' fees.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2
`the Arbitration Law governs the erosion arbitrators' fees` MEANS FALSE

§§ `6 תחולת חוק הבוררות`

-- §6: the Arbitration Law applies to this arbitration, save where the
-- parties agreed otherwise. The law is not in the corpus.
@ref akn:art_6 akn:art_6/p1
`why the Arbitration Law is not read here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק הבוררות"

§§ `7 מיצוי תביעות`

-- §7: the deed exhausts the parties' claims on the matters it settles.
@ref akn:art_7 akn:art_7/p1
`the erosion arbitration deed exhausts the claims on what it settles` MEANS TRUE

-- §8: the deed is the full application of the 1993–1995 agreements on the
-- rate of erosion and how it is computed, for 1.1.99–31.12.06; subject to
-- that, it takes nothing from those agreements' force.
@ref akn:art_8
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deed settles the 1993–1995 agreements' erosion for` y IF
    `a year the erosion arbitration covers` y

`the erosion arbitration deed takes force from the 1993–1995 agreements beyond it` MEANS FALSE

